<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chernobyl disaster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chernobyl disaster was the explosion and fire at reactor No. 4 of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in the Ukrainian SSR on 26 April 1986, the worst accident in the history of nuclear power. Radioactive fallout spread over much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> worst affected, and more than 100,000 people were evacuated from the zone around the plant. Initial Soviet secrecy damaged trust in the government and fed national movements.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chernobyl-disaster.jpg" alt="Chernobyl disaster" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: IAEA Imagebank · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IAEA_02790015_(5613115146).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
